 - Command-line switches (#48): the install family is parsed exactly like upstream (`-install <path>`, `-install-options <opts>`, `-uninstall [path]`, `-appdata`/`-noappdata`, `-startmenu`/`-nostartmenu`, `-isrunas`, and `<ext>`/`-no<ext>` for the nine associations — case-insensitive, run before the window exists; #26), then the second pass runs over the raw command line once the window exists — at startup and on every single-instance handoff — with upstream's own `string_get_word` tokenizer (quotes group words, `""` embeds a literal quote — NOT `CommandLineToArgvW`'s backslash rules — and a word is a switch only when UNQUOTED, `/`- or `-`-prefixed, and dot-free, so `-foo.png` is a file; a quoted `"/slideshow"` is a file too). The switch family: `/slideshow`, `/fullscreen`, `/window`, `/maximized` (the `/fullscreen /maximized` hybrid included), `/x /y /width /height` (unset axes keep the current rect), `/rate <index>`, the sort family `/name /path /size /dm /dc /ascending /descending`, `/shuffle`, `/add` (append — takes only when something is loaded), `/everything <term>` and `/random <term>` (fire the search on arrival), `/isrunas` (ignored), and the parameter words of every valued switch are consumed — nothing leaks into the file arguments anymore. Unknown switches pop the command-line usage box, which Help → Command Line Options opens too; upstream quirks kept: the `/appdata`/`/startmenu` words (install-pass citizens with no second-pass arm) pop that same usage box, `/rate` stores the slideshow PRESET INDEX while the usage text says "milliseconds" (upstream's own doc/impl mismatch), and `string_to_int` skips non-digits without stopping ("1x2" is 12). Divergences: the usage boxes pop after the whole line is applied (upstream pops per unknown word mid-parse — a modal box over a half-applied line is reentrancy upstream survives by accident), the body is localized (upstream hardcodes English; the exe name is brand-swapped), and `/ontop` `/minimal` `/compact` run their View commands in place exactly like upstream (#46 — On Top→Always through the toggle semantics, Minimal/Compact through the preset rows).
-- Upstream's default-on decode-ahead (preload next) and single-slot last-image cache (#40, `preload_next`/`cache_last` ini keys + the View-page checkboxes, both default on): after a load ends, the navigation neighbor (following the last MANUAL navigation's direction) decodes in the background and parks — navigating onto it swaps the parked frames in without a decode, and the previous display parks in the last slot so navigating back is instant. Cache discipline follows upstream: every sort change clears both caches (shuffle also re-preloads when idle), a repeat request of the in-flight file is a no-op, the last cache only accepts fully decoded displays, and the preloaded file is never the last cache's file. Two deliberate deviations from upstream's load-thread races: upstream's completion handler chains a queued open and then lets `preload_next` TERMINATE that just-started load (viv.c:2866-2877 — a drop/CLI open during a load can lose its display), while riviv's FIFO job queue runs the chained load to completion and preloads after it; and a system-level (GDI) decode failure in a PARKED preload degrades to dropping that preload instead of failing the process (upstream reports it as a user-level load failure too), keeping the fail-loud posture for the foreground path.
